d 'LUMPAPELL': module to perform Lumsdaine-Papell unit root test allowing for two unknown breaks
d
d    lumpapell implements the Lumsdaine-Papell unit root test,
d allowing for two breaks in the intercept, the trend or both at
d unknown locations (Lumsdaine & Papell, Review of Economics and
d Statistics, 1997). Four break specifications are available. Model
d AA lets both breaks shift the intercept; model CC lets each break
d shift both the intercept and the slope; model CA is the mixed
d case, in which the first break shifts the intercept and the slope
d and the second shifts the intercept only; and finally the
d break(trend) specification, which the article does not consider,
d lets each break shift the slope only. Lag lengths can be fixed or
d selected by information criteria or by the sequential t-test of
d Perron (1989). The command also writes the break dummies to the
d dataset and prints a plain regress command that reproduces the
d break regression. 
d
d KW: unit root tests
d KW: structural breaks
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author: Ozan Eruygur,  Ankara Haci Bayram Veli University
d Support: email eruygur@@gmail.com
d
f lumpapell.ado
f lumpapell.sthlp
